<Base title="Tracking Data to Basketball Events | Bence Supola"><div class="container"><div class="case-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Case study 02 · Data engineering / Event extraction</div><h1>Turning Tracking Data into Meaningful Events</h1><p class="lead">Extracting and validating basketball actions from high-frequency spatio-temporal data to study the role of secondary assists.</p><div class="skills"><span class="skill">Python</span><span class="skill">Event detection</span><span class="skill">Data validation</span><span class="skill">Statistical analysis</span></div></div><div class="prose"><h2>The challenge</h2><p>Raw tracking data captures positions, not basketball meaning. To analyze secondary assists, relevant passes, shots and sequences first had to be identified from player and ball trajectories and aligned with play-by-play information.</p><h2>The approach</h2><p>The research developed custom event-extraction logic and operational definitions to transform raw observations into analyzable basketball actions. Extracted events were evaluated against annotated reference material before being used for the substantive analysis.</p></div><figure class="figure"><img src="/images/secondary-pass-detection.png" alt="Ball position trajectories: black points mark other positions and colored segments mark detected passes." loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Unpublished pass-recognition visualization from ball-position tracking data. Colored segments indicate detected passes; black points show other ball positions.</figcaption></figure><div class="prose"><h2>What this demonstrates</h2><p>Event extraction, multi-source data integration, explicit operational definitions, validation of algorithmic outputs and statistical modeling — transferable skills for any setting where raw sensor streams must be converted into meaningful events.</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/24748668.2022.2039090">Read the peer-reviewed paper ↗</a></p><p><a href="/#work">← Back to selected work</a></p></div><figure class="figure"><img src="/images/secondary-inside-out.png" alt="Basketball court diagram displaying spatial connections in an inside-out pattern." loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Unpublished inside-out pattern visualization illustrating spatial relationships in the analysis. Colors and connections are shown as generated; no unverified category labels are assigned.</figcaption></figure></div></Base>
